  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to \\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x)-\\sqrt{3}}{2}=$\n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "Substituting $x=\\frac{\\pi }{6}$ directly into the limit, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to \\pi /6}\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3x)-\\sqrt{3}}{2} & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(3\\cdot \\frac{\\pi }{6})-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\operatorname{cot}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})-\\sqrt{3}}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{2})}-\\sqrt{3})}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{0}{1}-\\sqrt{3})}{2} \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
